{"id":246,"flavor":[{"games":["Shield","LeafGreen","Gold"],"text":"It feeds on soil. After it has eaten a large mountain, it will fall asleep so it can grow."},{"games":["Sword","Y","White 2","Black 2"],"text":"Born deep underground, it comes aboveground and becomes a pupa once it has finished eating the surrounding soil."},{"games":["Ultra Moon"],"text":"Raised on nutrients it finds in the dirt, it eats roughly a mountain’s worth of dirt before it becomes a pupa."},{"games":["Ultra Sun"],"text":"Born underground, it eats its way through dirt to the surface, where its parents are. It doesn’t deal well with the bright light it finds there."},{"games":["Alpha Sapphire","Omega Ruby"],"text":"Larvitar is born deep under the ground. To come up to the surface, this Pokémon must eat its way through the soil above. Until it does so, Larvitar cannot see its parents."},{"games":["X","HeartGold"],"text":"It feeds on soil. After it has eaten a large mountain, it falls asleep so it can grow."},{"games":["White","Black","Platinum","Pearl","Diamond"],"text":"A Pokémon that eats soil. Once it has eaten a large mountain, it goes to sleep so it can grow."},{"games":["SoulSilver","FireRed","Silver"],"text":"It is born deep underground. It can’t emerge until it has entirely consumed the soil around it."},{"games":["Emerald"],"text":"A LARVITAR is born deep under the ground. It must eat its way through the soil above and reach the surface for it to see its parents’ faces."},{"games":["Sapphire","Ruby"],"text":"LARVITAR is born deep under the ground. To come up to the surface, this POKéMON must eat its way through the soil above. Until it does so, LARVITAR cannot see its parent’s face."},{"games":["Crystal"],"text":"Born deep underground, this POKéMON becomes a pupa after eating enough dirt to make a mountain."}],"abilities":[{"name":"Guts","hidden":false,"description":"It's so gutsy that having a status condition boosts the Pokémon's Attack stat."},{"name":"Sand Veil","hidden":true,"des